{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792514622,"nonce":"eNve/x3Qif6CBLBiYdiRlT8Y+wM=","title":"LSP rejects inline markup before initialization macros can transform it","message":"RayDE's build.hxml configures ashui.ui.Markup.enable(), which uses Compiler.addGlobalMetadata to attach a build macro. Welcome.hx contains inline markup expressions. The current LSP rejects '\u003c' before expansion and returns only keywords, with null hover and document symbols.\n\nThe LSP drops --macro entries from hxml and library extraParams, and Rayzor's lexer does not produce Haxe's @:markup string expression. Initialization macros and their compiler effects must be evaluated generically; no project-specific markup transformation belongs in the server.\n\nReproduce against /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/RayDE using /tmp/rayzor-lsp-rayde/probe.py. Baseline protocol output is /tmp/rayzor-lsp-rayde/baseline.log. Also requested: when RAYZOR_STD_PATH is unset, LSP analysis should discover the installed Haxe stdlib (HAXE_STD_PATH and the Haxe installation), rather than requiring Rayzor's bundled library.","files":null}]}